When I used to play Nethack on the Linux graphical client, my stats
(STR, etc) appeared highlighted for a turn (in inverse) whenever they
increased or decreased. I liked this.

I've recently started playing again, using the TTY mode (in Putty on
Windows, thank the recent dev null tourney for me putting up with tty
long enough to learn to love it) However, these highlights to my stats
don't seem to appear in this mode, and I miss them for the following
reasons:

a. They provide prominent warning whenever a stat drops. It's too easy
not to notice a stat which drops for a subtle reason.

b. Providing immediate visual feedback helped me as a player associate
the changes in my stats with the action the caused the change, thus
helps me learn what's going on, and why.

c. Highlighting stats as they increase gives a more palpable and
immediate cause for celebration every time something good happens to
them.

I don't remember if changes to things like HP or AC are also
highlighted on the Linux graphical client, but for the purposes of this
discussion I'm proposing that they all should be.

I'm relatively new to Nethack compared to many on this list. Is this a
worthwhile suggestion? Or is manually keeping meticulous track of your
stats considered to be part of the zen of tty that I should simply get
on board with?

